   {
    "name": "Extended Reality at Berkeley",
    "position": "Event Horizon Team Lead · Jan 2019 - Dec 2019",
    "dateRange": {},
    "description": "Led an 8 person team in design and development of a sci-fi, escape room themed VR game in Unity Engine using the Oculus Rift SDK and Virtual Reality Toolkit. As a team lead I managed team meetings and member task assignment to ensure steady progress and ability to meet team goals using tools such as Monday. I also built various 3-d models for use as assets using Autodesk Maya. Finally I implemented scripts for in game events and the player using C# within Unity."
   },
   {
    "name": "Cal Convergent",
    "position": "Campus Solutions Team Member · Jan 2019 - May 2019",
    "dateRange": {},
    "description": "I was a member of the campus solutions project team for Cal Convergent. I worked with a team of 7 to design a product for the purpose of improving life on campus. We came up with Sharrand, an app where you can help other people when you are already running errands for yourself, or find another user to help you run your errands if they are conveniently already running a similar errand. I mainly worked on backend development of the app using React Native and Javascript, making the account creation and user profile pages and linking them with Firebase."
   }
